  "description": "Three stacked post-money SAFEs: cap-only, cap+discount, and MFN. Demonstrates YC 2018 iterative denominator + MFN sibling inference. Existing 10M common, Series A $2M @ $10M pre-money.",
  "derivation": "PPS = 10M / 10M = $1.00. SAFE C is MFN with no explicit terms → inherits best-for-investor sibling terms: cap = min(5M,10M) = 5M, discount = max(null,20%) = 20%. All three SAFEs use the YC 2018 self-referential post-money denom D = 10M + (SAFE A + B + C shares). SAFE B always picks discount ($0.80) = 312,500 shares (invariant of D since discount doesn't depend on D). SAFE A and C pick cap (5M/D < 0.80 when D > 6.25M). Fixed point: D = 10M + 500k×D/5M + 312,500 + 100k×D/5M = 10M + 0.12D + 312,500 → 0.88D = 10,312,500 → D ≈ 11,718,750. SAFE A shares = 500k × 11,718,748 / 5M = 1,171,874 (floor with iteration rounding). SAFE C shares = 100k × 11,718,748 / 5M = 234,374. Final FD = 10M + 1,171,874 + 312,500 + 234,374 + 2,000,000 = 13,718,748.",
